WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.040
In 1959, the young Dalai Lama
fled from Tibet to India.

2
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:09.230
In 1966, a Vietnamese Zen
monk, Thich Nhat Hanh,

3
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.060
went into exile too.

4
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.020
Two monks, two lost homelands.

5
00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:17.660
Both became refugees,
and prolific authors.

6
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:22.080
So how did two monks driven from their
homelands become Buddhism's best-known

7
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.810
voices in the West?

8
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.430
In this mission, you'll trace
their two lives side by side,

9
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.780
from exile to world fame.

10
00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.860
Then you'll find the key note
that each of them sounds,

11
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:36.180
again and again, in everything he teaches.

12
00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:41.330
Your mission: explain how two exiled
monks found such a hearing in the West.
